onally, it is served as a wedding soup and is introduced between courses of meat, intended to boost digestion."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dovga"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dovga"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Azerbaijani cuisine","cuisine/azerbaijani-cuisine"],["Uzbek cuisine","cuisine/uzbek-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":9,"links":[["Coriander","ingredient/coriander"],["Dill","ingredient/dill"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Mentha","ingredient/mentha"],["Qatiq","ingredient/qatiq"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Spinach","ingredient/spinach"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yogurt","ingredient/yogurt"]]},{"h":"More from Azerbaijani cuisine","links":[["Badambura","dish/badambura"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Doghramaj","dish/doghramaj"],["Eggplant jam","dish/eggplant-jam"],["Khash (dish)","dish/khash-dish"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Scorched rice","dish/scorched-rice"],["Shekerbura","dish/shekerbura"],["Sheki halva","dish/sheki-halva"],["Shorgoghal","dish/shorgoghal"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/f8/Dovga_e-citizen.JPG/500px-Dovga_e-citizen.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Moonsun1981","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dovga_e-citizen.JPG"}},"dish/frigarui":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/frigarui","n":"Frigărui","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Romanian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Frigărui is a Romanian dish consisting of small pieces of meat (usually pork, beef, mutton, lamb or chicken) grilled on a skewer, similar to shashlik or shish kebab. Often, the pieces of meat alternate with bacon, sausages, or vegetables, such as onions, tomatoes, bell peppers and mushrooms. It is seasoned with spices such as pepper, garlic, savory, rosemary, marjoram and laurel."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-frigarui"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frig%C4%83rui"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Romanian cuisine","cuisine/romanian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Notes from Irina's Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"irinageorgescu.substack.com","note":"Newsletter of Romanian recipes and food stories from cookbook author Irina Georgescu.","url":"https://irinageorgescu.substack.com/about","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Romanian cuisine","links":[["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Ostropel","dish/ostropel"],["Papanași","dish/papanasi"],["Sarmale","dish/sarmale"],["Scorcolga","dish/scorcolga"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"],["Taramasalata","dish/taramasalata"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/bd/Frig%C4%83rui.jpg/500px-Frig%C4%83rui.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Premus","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frig%C4%83rui.jpg"}},"dish/frittata":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/frittata","n":"Frittata","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Frittata is an egg-based Italian dish, similar to an omelette, crustless quiche or scrambled eggs, enriched with additional ingredients such as meats, cheeses or vegetables."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-frittata"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frittata"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-su